{
  "summary": "The experiment tested a basic multimodal setup combining RNA data encoded with pca_n2000 and image data encoded with resnet50 via simple concatenation. Validation accuracy of 0.5266 and F1 score of 0.5104 suggest multimodal integration achieved comparable performance to single-modal baselines, though this remains an initial observation without direct comparison. The impact of the fusion method on performance cannot be isolated due to the absence of alternative fusion strategies for comparison."
}

